description: Prefer serialized references over Find/GetComponent
alwaysApply: true
---

# No scene search

Do not use `FindObjectOfType`, `FindObjectsOfType`, or `GameObject.Find` in runtime gameplay code. Do not call `GetComponent` / `GetComponentInChildren` every frame or to look up scene objects.

Wire references in the Inspector (or through [ExperimentSceneRefs](Assets/Scripts/ExperimentSceneRefs.cs)). Cache a component only at spawn time, when you just added it.

```csharp
// BAD
var hud = FindObjectOfType<HUDController>();
var bike = GameObject.Find("bicyle_animated_human");
void Update() { GetComponent<NavMeshAgent>().speed = 8f; }

// GOOD
[SerializeField] HUDController hud;
[SerializeField] Transform bicycle;
void Awake() { _agent = agentAssignedAtSpawn; }
```

Allowed exceptions: Editor menus, one-time bind of empty Inspector fields on `ExperimentSceneRefs`, `AddComponent` immediately after `Instantiate`.
